WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.000
Unit 3 is who can do what.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.373
Microsoft Learn describes four permission
groups in Defender's unified role-based

3
00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:10.903
access control: security
operations, security posture,

4
00:00:10.903 --> 00:00:14.050
authorization and settings,
and data operations.

5
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:18.537
The program builds four roles from them;
that's its risk-based recommendation.

6
00:00:18.537 --> 00:00:21.136
A read role, called Security data basics,

7
00:00:21.136 --> 00:00:24.363
for analysts and the
assessor's read-only account.

8
00:00:24.363 --> 00:00:29.025
A responder role that adds alerts,
response and basic live response.

9
00:00:29.025 --> 00:00:32.382
A detection engineer role
with Detection tuning,

10
00:00:32.382 --> 00:00:35.575
manage, which the custom
detection A P I accepts.

11
00:00:35.575 --> 00:00:39.238
And advanced live response
only for Tier zero analysts.

12
00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:43.737
Each role is assigned to groups that pim
governs, so no one holds it standing.

13
00:00:43.737 --> 00:00:48.012
Create every role and assignment
before you activate the workloads;

14
00:00:48.012 --> 00:00:52.587
Learn says activation needs at least
Security Administrator in Entra I D.

15
00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:55.512
Then connect the S O C's read path.

16
00:00:55.512 --> 00:00:59.549
Learn names Security Incident dot
Read dot All as the least-privileged

17
00:00:59.549 --> 00:01:04.063
permission to list incidents, and Threat
Hunting dot Read dot All to run queries.

18
00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:08.920
Connect with the environment
of the tenant's cloud:

19
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.662
Global for G C C, U S Gov for G C
C High, U S Gov D O D for D O D.

20
00:01:13.662 --> 00:01:16.796
A session in the wrong
cloud returns an empty list,

21
00:01:16.796 --> 00:01:19.010
and an empty list looks like a pass.
